# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# backend/.gitignore
#
# WHY DO WE NEED THIS FILE?
#   Git tracks all files in your project by default.
#   However, some files should NEVER be uploaded or shared on GitHub:
#
#   1. node_modules/ → Contains thousands of downloaded library files.
#                      Anyone who clones your repository can easily recreate
#                      this folder by simply running 'npm install'.
#
#   2. .env          → Stores sensitive environment variables (such as secret keys,
#                      database passwords, and port configurations).
#                      Keeping it ignored prevents accidental security leaks.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Environment Variables & Secrets
.env
.env.local

# Logs
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
